course: dictionary
lesson: 12469
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word deflection can mean a change in direction, a bending or moving aside, or turning attention away from something. «The ball went in off a deflection» means it bounced off a player and changed direction.
explain: In science, a deflection is how far something bends or moves aside when a force pushes on it. «The deflection of the compass needle» tells us how strongly a magnet is pulling it. The more the needle moves, the bigger the deflection.
explain: When someone avoids a hard question by changing the subject, we call it a deflection. «Mia was asked why she was late, so she talked loudly about the weather. That was a deflection.» Mia moved attention away from herself. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Deflection means a change in direction, or a bending or moving aside.
fact: In sport, a goal scored off a deflection changed direction when it hit another player.
fact: In science, deflection is how much something bends or moves aside under a force, like a compass needle.
fact: Deflection can also mean turning attention, blame or a question away from yourself.
fact: Phrases to spot: «a lucky deflection», «a deflection off», «deflection of the needle».
exercise: «The shot hit a defender and went in off a deflection.» What does deflection mean here? | A pass to a teammate | *A change in direction after hitting something | A missed penalty kick | A loud cheer from the crowd
exercise: «The needle on the meter showed a big deflection when the magnet came close.» What is the deflection? | The needle being taken out of the box | The magnet losing its power | *The needle moving aside under the magnet's pull | The meter breaking
exercise: «When Mia was asked why she was late, she talked about the weather.» Her talking was a... | *Deflection, moving the question away from herself | Measurement | Race | Penalty
test: «The light beam showed a clear deflection after it passed through the glass prism.» What does deflection mean here? | Getting brighter | *Bending or moving aside | Stopping completely | Turning off
test: «Dad asked who broke the cup, and Leo's loud joke was a deflection.» What does deflection suggest? | *Leo was turning attention away from himself | Leo was going to bed | Leo was telling the truth | Leo was asking for help
exam: Which sentence uses deflection to mean turning attention away from yourself? | The ball took a lucky deflection off the post. | The needle showed a deflection of ten degrees. | *When asked who ate the cake, Sam changed the subject, which was a deflection.
